<title>INDIA: BSE figures of India carry forward trade - March 15.</title>
<headline>BSE figures of India carry forward trade - March 15.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the latest data, for the top 10 stocks by value, released by the Bombay Stock Exchange (BSE) for the carry forward or &quot;badla&quot; account ended March 15</p>
<p>SCRIP		  SETTLEMENT  AV BADLA  QTY    VALUE   % BADLA</p>
<p>			 RATE				(RS MLN)</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Reliance	     280	   1.93     749500  209.86   35.94</p>
<p>State Bank	   305	   2.10     562100  171.44   35.90</p>
<p>Tata Steel	   189	   1.33     634750  119.97   36.69</p>
<p>ITC		    430	   2.96     226700   97.48   35.89</p>
<p>BSES		   220	   1.52     274200   60.32   36.03</p>
<p>L&amp;T		    255	   1.64     233300   59.49   33.54</p>
<p>Tata Engg	    385	   2.73     114400   44.04   36.97</p>
<p>MTNL		   285	   1.97     142400   40.58   36.04</p>
<p>ACC		   1670	  11.66	22840   38.14   36.41</p>
<p>Arvind Mills	 141	   0.97     258650   36.47   35.87</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>The average badla charges work out to 36.57 percent on an annualised basis against 45.08 percent in the previous carry forward account ended March 8.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
